WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:05.560
Hey Youtubers it's Charlie and this is going
to be my review of How to Train Your Dragon

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.560
2.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.270
I think it's only a coincidence that Kit Harington
is in the movie and Game of Thrones finale

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:14.059
is this weekend but it made the movie extra
fun to watch.

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:17.270
Since most of you probably haven't seen the
movie I'm going to start with my non-spoilery

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:22.340
review then I'll get into specific top 5 moments
and talk about where the sequels are going.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.560
That's right, they're talking about doing
four movies instead of just three.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.914
If you're finding me for the first time, since
it's the summer movie season I'm doing weekly

00:00:28.914 --> 00:00:31.320
reviews of the big stuff I'm really excited
about.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.210
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.230
Next up is 22 Jump Street and Transformers.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:38.720
It's like a whole summer of sequels, and normally
that's not good news.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.690
A lot of sequels in the past have just turned
up the explosions to eleven at the expense

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:43.690
of the characters.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:48.180
But one of my favorite things about How To
Train Your Dragon was how it changed the characters.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.070
Especially toothless, Hiccups nightfury.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.370
Going into the movie I knew they'd be doing
two more movies, so I kept wondering how the

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.390
story would set those up.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:57.340
I'll talk more about that during spoilers.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.309
Like I said, Kit Harington joined the cast,
Cate Blanchett and Djimon Honsou.

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:04.760
Of all the newcomers Cate Blanchett really
stood out but that's not really fair, Kit

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:09.389
Harington does a lot better when you can see
him and Djimon Honsou's character, the villain

00:01:09.389 --> 00:01:12.149
isn't quite up to Turbo Wreck It Ralph standards.

00:01:12.149 --> 00:01:19.509
In case you didn't know the movies are based
on books written by Cressida Cowell.

00:01:19.509 --> 00:01:23.880
Dreamworks liked the first movie so much they
asked the movie writer Dean DeBlois to write

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:24.880
the sequel.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:25.880
And he said yes only on the condition that
he could do a trilogy.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.049
He specifically cited Star Wars the original
Trilogy as inspiration.

00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:44.419
So if this feels like Empire Strikes Back
with all the ice and Hoth and missing limbs,

00:01:44.419 --> 00:01:45.459
that's why.

00:01:45.459 --> 00:01:48.929
Which makes me wonder now if the third film
will feel like Return of The Jedi?

00:01:48.929 --> 00:01:51.189
I totally don't mind if it's an overt homage.

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:56.389
The Empire Strikes Back of the How To Train
Your Dragon takes that idea of trying to understand

00:01:56.389 --> 00:02:02.399
your enemies and takes it to a much darker
place.

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:06.630
The story definitely got a lot darker than
the first movie but I would have like to learn

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.399
more about Djimon Hansou's character.

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:09.569
Drago Bludvist.

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:13.110
The movie is only about an hour and forty
minutes long, so it almost feels short enough

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:14.630
to be a tv movie.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:21.220
I don't know if any of you have seen it, but
there is a tv show based on the first movie

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:24.141
called Dragon Riders of Berk, it only stars
a couple people from the movies, most of the

00:02:24.141 --> 00:02:26.000
main cast members aren't in it.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.560
The other big improvement in the sequel is
the animation.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.620
Because the technology evolves so fast and
this is one of Dreamworks biggest movies they

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.620
really went all out.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.391
It's like at E3 this week when they were showing
off demos of Dragon Age Inquisition with crazy

00:02:35.391 --> 00:02:36.840
awesome graphics cards on huge screens.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.180
The images are so rich with detail it kind
of melts your face a little.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:44.500
It gave them the ability to make Toothless
move in some really fun new ways.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.680
The dragons are some of the biggest actors
in the movie and their performance is completely

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:49.990
dependent on the animation.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:52.150
And I thought they did an awesome job.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:56.800
After you go see the movie though, make sure
to watch the Game of Thrones finale on Sunday

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:57.800
for an extra special treat.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.420
It's just fun seeing Kit Harington on two
things with dragons.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:00.980
So time to get into spoilers, careful if you
haven't seen the movie yet but I'm going to

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:06.340
do my top 5 moments and then talk about the
sequels.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.470
Here we go, Number 5 - Hiccup Is Building
a Map

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:12.790
This is going to serve as the device that
takes them through the future sequels.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:16.650
It's like in Pirates of the Caribbean 3 when
they yanked out that map at the end.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.130
Hiccup is going to continue to chart the known
world.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.310
They even said it in the movie, with Dragons
around, the world just got a whole lot bigger.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:26.720
Technically it should have been that Dragons
allow them to travel farther, so the world

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.200
is getting smaller.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.000
But you get the idea, their world before the
first movie was just that little island of

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:36.460
Berk and now they're going further and further
out and meeting all these new characters.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.590
Number 4 - The Alpha Sanctuary

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:40.830
Definitely the coolest new location in the
movie.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:45.090
I know I said the writer was inspired by the
Star Wars Trilogy, but I also saw a lot of

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:48.040
Star Trek Wrath of Kahn when they entered
the cave.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.170
He meets his mother and they travel to Hoth,
the ice planet.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:55.190
But she takes him inside her secret garden
cave like Carol Marcus in Wrath of Kahn.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:04:00.090
I totally love it when animated movies and
cartoons can pay homage to big science fiction

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.840
movies and it doesn't feel cheesy.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.840
The animation inside the cave made my face
melt a little.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:08.920
Especially that reveal moment when Hiccup
sees all the dragons for the first time and

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:12.250
they're all flying in formation around the
ice pillar.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:13.540
Meeting the Alpha was pretty amazing too.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:17.340
It felt like a big step up from the mega dragon
of the first movie.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:20.219
Number 3 - Hiccup Starts to Learn More Dragonlore

00:04:20.219 --> 00:04:24.080
There were a ton of new things the movie taught
us about dragons and controlling dragons.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:27.669
It seems like his mother Cate Blanchett's
character is going to be teaching him all

00:04:27.669 --> 00:04:28.669
of the new things.

00:04:28.669 --> 00:04:33.419
I also got a flash of Game of Thrones from
Season 3 with the Control Rod Daenerys got

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:35.719
that controlled the unsullied army.

00:04:35.719 --> 00:04:40.919
Hiccups mom and Drago both had those Dragon
control staffs which presumably Hiccup will

00:04:40.919 --> 00:04:43.410
learn to use too.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:47.160
There were a few big questions I had about
those.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.900
If Drago was doing the same thing as Hiccup's
Mom, why couldn't she command the evil alpha

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:52.939
like Drago?

00:04:52.939 --> 00:04:57.560
Part of the story was about bonding with dragons
on a really deep level rather than just ordering

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.110
them around like mindless zombies.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:05.669
The movie didn't make it clear why Drago was
the only one able to control his alpha.

00:05:05.669 --> 00:05:08.439
Number 2 - Hiccups Mom and Dad are Reunited

00:05:08.439 --> 00:05:12.130
I should have seen that this was writing on
the wall for Gerard Butler's character dying.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:14.559
At least he got to dance with her one last
time.

00:05:14.559 --> 00:05:18.210
Even though you'd expect Hiccup and his relationship
with Toothless or even Astrid to be the core

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.460
emotional moment of the film.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:22.860
I felt like his parents singing and dancing
together was the most cry worthy scene.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.629
How dare you make me cry Gerard Butler and
Cate Blanchett.

00:05:25.629 --> 00:05:26.930
They were both really good singers.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:30.289
I didn't think they needed to add Craig Ferguson's
character in that scene.

00:05:30.289 --> 00:05:32.580
I didn't think they needed jokes to break
the tension

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:44.180
and my Number 1 moment - Toothless Saves Hiccup
From the Alpha

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:48.069
I always thought the dragons behaved more
like Dogs than any other animal, so it totally

00:05:48.069 --> 00:05:50.509
made sense the way they incorporated pack
mentality.

00:05:50.509 --> 00:05:54.879
Like you have an alpha that has a level of
social control over the weaker dragons but

00:05:54.879 --> 00:05:58.870
another dragon or dog, can come along and
challenge for control.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:05:59.870
Enter Toothless.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:04.979
I loved the way they paid off the bits about
dragonlore and toothless's new abilities.

00:06:04.979 --> 00:06:09.360
Remember, they told us he's the same age as
hiccup, so of course he's going to be developing

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.539
new abilities as he matures.

00:06:11.539 --> 00:06:14.430
The one big bummer was that we didn't see
any other night furies.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:18.960
But now it's your turn, let me know what your
favorite moment was and where do you want

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.669
them to go in the sequels.

00:06:20.669 --> 00:06:24.870
Just going on the Star Wars metaphor, they'd
have to go to a forest or a jungle.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:29.330
I think what we'll see is a new colony of
Night Furies, it's like during Kung Fu Panda

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.889
3 where they found all the other Pandas.

00:06:31.889 --> 00:06:35.139
Which is kind of funny, because that was Dreamworks
last big animated franchise.

00:06:35.139 --> 00:06:37.509
So of course they'd do that plot again.

00:06:37.509 --> 00:06:42.150
Only in this case Toothless thinks he's the
only Panda left or Night Fury, however you

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.150
want to think about it.

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:47.529
But the things that really stood out to me
as teasers for the sequels were Hiccups mom

00:06:47.529 --> 00:06:52.300
teaching him new things about dragons, Hiccup
charting the big map and Toothless being the

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:56.990
last Night Fury.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:07:09.029
So, like I said, Game of Thrones with more
Kit Harington this sunday.

00:07:09.029 --> 00:07:14.319
My next movie review will probably be 22 Jump
Street but at least Transformers.

